KZ2 2158, from Killzone 3 patch 2158 (port/patches/2158-perf-texreg-stability.patch; same owner).
Counter-only texture register stability profile (RSX_PERF_TEXREG=1, default off, with RSX_PERF=1 RSX_PERF_PROF=A,B).

Compares the 16 units' 9 raw texture words of each draw with the previous draw's inside the RSX_PERF_PROF window and
prints [perf-texreg] when the window closes: draws with all units unchanged, with every enabled and used unit
unchanged, per-unit change rates, and enabled units split into same / offset-only / other. No decision reads it.
Adapted for KZ2: KZ2 has no 2136 texture memo, so ld_trg_raw reads the same 9 words KZ3's
ld_tm_raw returns (0x1A00 + u*0x20, 8 words, and control3 0x1840 + u*4) from the dispatch state; the counter sits
before KZ2's texture bind loop.

